    "message": "feat(reasoning): offer adaptive thinking as a per-tier choice\n\nAnthropic's adaptive extended thinking already worked -- the Messages\nprovider defaults to thinking {\"type\":\"adaptive\"} when nothing else is\nspecified -- but there was no way to ASK for it. A tier could be Off,\nFrom client, or a fixed effort, and nothing else.\n\nThis adds Adaptive alongside them, so a tier can hand the decision back\nto the model per request instead of pinning one effort for every call.\n\nAdaptive is carried as its own ReasoningControl member rather than\noverloading an existing one, because it is a third intent: DEFAULT means\nno opinion was expressed, ON means reasoning was demanded (optionally at\na named effort), and ADAPTIVE means the model should choose. Collapsing\nit into either would lose the distinction the request log needs to record\nand the Anthropic encoder needs to act on.\n\n`requests_reasoning` deliberately answers False for it: adaptive names no\neffort and no budget, so a generic encoder has nothing representable to\nsend and falls through to the provider's own default -- exactly today's\nbehaviour. Only an encoder that publishes an adaptive channel of its own\nacts on it, and only the Anthropic Messages provider does. No provider\ngains a new wire field.\n\nmodels.dev publishes no adaptive signal (its only reasoning_options types\nare effort, toggle and budget_tokens), so this cannot be capability-driven\nand is not pretending to be. Per-model gating still applies around it: a\nmodel known not to reason has reasoning suppressed even under an adaptive\ntier, and an unknown model is returned unchanged by identity, as always.\n\nNothing changes for anyone who does not select it. Anthropic's existing\ndefault-to-adaptive is untouched, and every other preference resolves\nexactly as before.\n\nVerification:\n- Independent probe: all eight preferences resolve correctly; adaptive\n  passes gating unchanged by object identity on unknown and effort-capable\n  models, and is suppressed on a model known not to reason; the option\n  renders in all five tier dropdowns with its label.\n- Mutation-tested: deleting the manifest label entry raises KeyError at\n  import across 32 tests, so the option cannot be added to the enum\n  without reaching the UI.\n- Full suite 4747 passed, 6 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty check clean repo-wide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
